Identify the category or classification of the VS-300 based on historical and technical context.
The Vought-Sikorsky VS-300 is classified as a single-engine helicopter with a single vertical-plane tail rotor configuration, making it the first successful helicopter in the United States to use this design. It is also recognized as the first practical amphibious helicopter due to its floats attachment capability. Additionally, it is historically significant as the first successful single lifting rotor helicopter.
