Identify the international registration requirements and format for vehicles originating from Belize, including the specific alphanumeric code system used for international vehicle registration.
The international registration requirements for vehicles originating from Belize include the use of an international licence plate country code. This code is part of the system maintained by the United Nations Economic Commission for Europe as the "Distinguishing Signs Used on Vehicles in International Traffic" (DSIT). The specific alphanumeric code used for Belize is "BZ." This code is displayed on the rear of the vehicle, either separately from the registration plate or incorporated into it. The code helps identify the issuing country of the vehicle registration plate for international traffic.
