Identify the chemical composition and common usage of laughing gas to determine its correct scientific and common names
The sub-question refers to "laughing gas," which is commonly known as nitrous oxide. Its chemical composition is **dinitrogen monoxide (N₂O)**. Nitrous oxide is a colorless, non-flammable gas that is used in various applications, including as an anesthetic in medical procedures and as a propellant in aerosol cans. It is also used in the food industry as a leavening agent. The scientific name for laughing gas is **nitrous oxide**, and its common name is **laughing gas**.
