Identify the terrorist group responsible for the kidnapping and murder of Italian Prime Minister Aldo Moro in 1978, including the historical context and key events of the operation.
The terrorist group responsible for the kidnapping and murder of Italian Prime Minister Aldo Moro in 1978 was the Red Brigades (Italian: "Brigate Rosse," or BR). This event, known as the Moro Case, marked a significant moment in Italian political history. On 16 March 1978, Moro, who was the former prime minister and president of the Christian Democracy (DC) party, was kidnapped by the Red Brigades. The operation occurred on the day when Moro was expected to undergo a confidence vote for a new cabinet led by Giulio Andreotti in the Italian Parliament. The kidnapping and subsequent murder of Moro were pivotal events that highlighted the tensions between the Italian government and leftist militant groups during the period of political instability in Italy. Valerio Morucci, a former member of the Red Brigades, was involved in the kidnapping and assassination. The incident had profound implications for Italian politics and security policies.
