The Dan Hodge Trophy is awarded to the most outstanding college wrestler of the year. It is given each season to the nation's best college wrestler by W.I.N. Magazine ("Wrestling Insider Newsmagazine") and Culture House. The trophy is awarded based on seven criteria: 1. Record, 2. Number of pins, 3. Dominance, 4. Past credentials, 5. Quality of competition, 6. Sportsmanship/citizenship, and 7. Heart. The trophy is the wrestling equivalent to the Heisman Trophy.
