River Phoenix died on October 31, 1993, at the age of 23 due to a drug overdose. The incident occurred outside a nightclub called the Viper Room, located on La Cienega Boulevard in Los Angeles. He collapsed and convulsed for over five minutes before being rushed to Cedars-Sinai Medical Center, where he was pronounced dead at 1:51 a.m. PST. The club became a makeshift shrine following his death, with fans and mourners leaving tributes on the premises.
