Determine which specific soap opera and episode first introduced the question 'Who shot JR?' and analyze its role in popularizing the phrase within the genre.
The question "Who shot JR?" first appeared in the soap opera *Dallas*, specifically in the episode titled "Who Shot J.R.?" which aired on November 21, 1980. This episode is widely regarded as one of the most memorable cliffhangers in television history. The dramatic and suspenseful ending, where the identity of the person who shot J.R. Ewing (the show's central character) was left unresolved, captivated audiences worldwide.

The episode's success played a significant role in popularizing the phrase "Who shot J.R.?" within the genre of soap operas and beyond. It became a cultural reference point, symbolizing the intense drama and unpredictability characteristic of the genre. The cliffhanger also contributed to the broader trend of using such endings to boost viewership and generate buzz, influencing the way television dramas are structured. The impact of this episode was so profound that it even led to a suspension of a session of the Turkish parliament to allow legislators to watch the conclusion, highlighting its global appeal and significance.
