In the UK, the equivalent of a "Secretary of State" is a higher-ranking role, often referred to as "Her Majesty's Principal Secretary of State for [specific department]." This title is used for senior ministers who oversee major government departments, such as the Foreign Secretary or the Chancellor of the Exchequer. The term "Secretary of State" is not used in the same way in all countries; it can denote various levels of government roles depending on the nation's system.
