Identify the name of the Earth's outermost layer and explain its composition and characteristics
The name of the Earth's outermost layer is the pedosphere. It is composed of soil and is subject to soil formation processes. The pedosphere exists at the interface of the lithosphere, atmosphere, hydrosphere, and biosphere. It is the foundation of terrestrial life on Earth and is characterized by its dynamic interaction with these other spheres. The pedosphere has the highest concentration of organic matter and microorganisms, where most of the Earth's biological soil activity occurs. It is composed of mineral particles, organic matter, water, and air.
