Describe the mechanism by which this reactive component interacts with ozone molecules in the stratosphere
The reactive component, chlorine atoms (Cl), interacts with ozone molecules (O₃) in the stratosphere through a catalytic cycle. Chlorine atoms react with ozone, removing one oxygen atom to form chlorine monoxide (ClO). ClO is also a radical and reacts with another ozone molecule, releasing two oxygen molecules and regenerating a chlorine atom. This process continues as the chlorine atom is not consumed, allowing it to repeatedly destroy ozone molecules. This mechanism contributes significantly to the depletion of the ozone layer.
