Define a furlong and determine its relationship to other units of length in the imperial system
A furlong is a unit of distance in the imperial and U.S. customary systems, equal to one-eighth of a mile. It is equivalent to 660 feet, 220 yards, 40 rods, or 10 chains. In terms of the international yard (exactly 0.9144 meters), one furlong is 201.168 meters. In the United States, which uses the U.S. survey foot, a furlong is approximately 201.1684 meters. The difference between the U.S. and international values is negligible for most practical purposes.
