Identify the year the Best Foreign Language Film category was first introduced to the Academy Awards, including its original name and any relevant historical context.
The Best Foreign Language Film category was first introduced to the Academy Awards in 1956 (29th Academy Awards). It was originally known as the "Academy Award of Merit" and was created specifically for non-English speaking films. Prior to this, between 1947 and 1955, the Academy presented Special/Honorary Awards to foreign language films, but these were not competitive and were given on an irregular basis. The new category marked the beginning of a competitive annual award for foreign language films.
